<Simple title="About this guide" seoTitle="About Best Cities in Spain | Independent City Guide" description="Who writes Best Cities in Spain, how we check facts, how the site makes money, and why we're not linked to any tourist board." path="/about/">
  <p class="lede">Best Cities in Spain is an independent English guide to eight Spanish cities for a first visit: Madrid, Barcelona, Seville, Granada, Valencia, Málaga, San Sebastián and Bilbao. It helps you choose between them, plan the trains and book the tickets that sell out.</p>
  <h2>Independent</h2>
  <p><strong>Independent travel guide, not affiliated with any Spanish tourist board.</strong> No city, hotel, museum or tour operator pays to appear here or to be ranked.</p>
  <h2>How we check facts</h2>
  <p>Every page shows the date it was last checked. Facts come from primary sources where they exist: the monuments' and museums' own sites, Renfe and the other train operators, the cities' tourist offices and UNESCO. Where a page gives a time or a price, it links to where we found it. Timetables and prices change, so check the operator's site before you travel.</p>
  <p>Tour prices and ratings are copied from GetYourGuide on the date shown next to them. They are GetYourGuide's prices, not ours.</p>
  <h2>How the site makes money</h2>
  <p>When you book a tour through a GetYourGuide link, or a stay through a Booking.com link, on this site, we may earn a commission. You pay the same price. See the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
</Simple>
